            <ArticleTitle>Perineal endometrioma occurring during pregnancy: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Perineal endometrioma has been reported in reproductive-aged women following perineal trauma. The common presentation is a perineal mass with cyclic pain coincident with the menstrual cycle in a woman with a history of perineal laceration. Curative treatment is possible with complete surgical excision. No reports of perineal endometrioma occurring during pregnancy have been published before.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CASE" NlmCategory="METHODS">A case of perineal endometrioma occurred during pregnancy. The patient had a perineal mass that enlarged, with worsening pain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">A perineal endometrioma may progress during pregnancy. Proper diagnosis is important, and treatment with surgical excision should be considered before attempting subsequent pregnancies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
